---
export const title = 'Dismissing and sticky';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>dismissible</code> adds a close button. Pressing it fires a cancelable <code>close</code> event
  with <code>detail.reason</code> <code>'action'</code>, then the banner hides itself (sets
  <code>hidden</code>). Call <code>preventDefault()</code> to keep it.
</p>
<p>
  <code>dismiss-key</code> remembers the dismissal in <code>localStorage</code> under
  <code>wc-banner:&lt;key&gt;</code>, so the banner stays hidden on later visits. Give each message its
  own key (for example <code>maintenance-2026-11-20</code>) so a new message shows again. When storage is
  blocked the banner just shows again next time.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%;'>
    <wc-banner id='banner-demo' intent='info' dismissible dismiss-key='docs-banner-demo' headline='Tip:'>
      Press the close button, then reload the page: the banner stays hidden.
    </wc-banner>
    <wc-button id='banner-reset' variant='text' size='sm' style='margin-top: 1rem;'>Forget dismissal</wc-button>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#banner-demo').addEventListener('close', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('close: ' + event.detail.reason);
    });
    document.querySelector('#banner-reset').addEventListener('click', function () {
      try {
        localStorage.removeItem('wc-banner:docs-banner-demo');
      } catch (e) {}
      document.querySelector('#banner-demo').hidden = false;
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  <code>sticky</code> keeps the banner at the top of its scroll container while the page scrolls
  (<code>position: sticky</code>); <code>--banner-z-index</code> sets its stacking order.
  <code>--banner-max-content-width</code> centers the content in a narrower column while the background
  stays full width.
</p>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>
<p>
  A banner is not a live region by default, so one that is there when the page loads is read in reading
  order, not announced. For a banner you add while the page is in use, set <code>live="polite"</code>
  (<code>role="status"</code>), or <code>live="assertive"</code> (<code>role="alert"</code>) for urgent
  news such as a lost connection. The close button is named by the <code>dismissBanner</code> string,
  translated with <code>setPeacockStrings()</code>.
</p>
